== B: charged-sector dressing requirement ==
  m_e/m_mu: x = 1.546; vs rung 1.5: C_req = 0.8529 (sqrt(1-k eps) k = +8.6); nearest attainable 0.8393 (off by 1.6%)
  m_mu/m_tau: x = 0.818; vs rung 0.5: C_req = 0.3335 (sqrt(1-k eps) k = +27.9); nearest attainable 0.6746 (off by 102.3%)
  m_mu/m_tau: x = 0.818; vs rung 1.0: C_req = 1.8699 (sqrt(1-k eps) k = -78.5); nearest attainable 1.9015 (off by 1.7%)
  charged masses are measured to <1e-4 relative, so a texture
  'hit' must match C_req essentially exactly; the gaps above are
  percent-level or worse -> within this texture class (2x2,
  exponents <= 2, unit coefficients) the charged steps are NOT
  reproduced.  The sector criterion is therefore a NAMED
  HYPOTHESIS, not a derivation: charged masses pass through EWSB
  seams (additional uncomputed dressing); the seesaw step is
  pre-EWSB ('D-shield').  Until the EWSB dressing is computed,
  the charged sector neither confirms nor calibrates the
  mechanism - counted against the program, not for it.

